  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0 - Major release: Gotenberg 9 support next to 7 and 8 (the client reads the service version and sends each request in the form that API takes), with explicit Gotenberg 9 stages. Native AOT and trimming support for .NET 8+; JSON uses source-generated System.Text.Json and the Newtonsoft.Json dependency is removed. Breaking: the built-in Polly retry is removed (add Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience to the returned IHttpClientBuilder), RetryPolicy.Enabled = true fails options validation, JObject parameters and properties are now IDictionary<string, object> or JsonObject, TimeoutHandler is removed, and TimeOut limits the whole call including the download. See CHANGES.MD for full details.\n      v3.3.0 - Standalone encrypt (Gotenberg 8.23.1+) and rotate (8.28.0+) check the server version first and throw GotenbergVersionNotSupportedException on older services instead of a 404. See CHANGES.MD for full details.\n      v3.2.1 - Retry fixes: settings on options subclasses are honoured, only connection failures, 429, 502 and 503 are retried, and non-seekable streams are not resent. GotenbergApiException exposes Trace and reads error bodies asynchronously. A-series paper sizes are exact. Options are validated. Implicit number-to-Dimension conversions are obsolete. See CHANGES.MD for full details.\n      v3.1.0 - PDF bookmark read/write support. Embed files into PDFs (ZUGFeRD / Factur-X). Gotenberg version compatibility checking with clear errors for unsupported features.\n      v3.0.0 - Major release: Screenshot operations (HTML/URL to PNG/JPEG/WebP). Standalone PDF engine operations (flatten, rotate, split, encrypt, metadata). Cross-cutting watermark, stamp, rotation, and split options. LibreOffice conversion options. PDF encryption. Additional Chromium fields. Dropped .NET 5/6/7; added .NET 9/10. Namespace reorganization (builders moved to Application layer). See CHANGES.MD for full details.\n      v2.8.5 - Added support for the GenerateTaggedPdf flag.\n      v2.8.4 - Fixed hybrid configuration for basic authentication credentials.\n      v2.8.3 - Added programmatic configuration support. Comprehensive documentation improvements.\n      v2.8.1 - Added cookie support, basic auth, SinglePage property.\n      v2.8 - PDF formatting improvements, flatten support.\n      v2.0 - Upgraded to support Gotenberg v7.",
